/*! \page Solver_intro C++ solver

\section Solver_intro_introduction Introduction

The production engine of RadCluster is a C++17 program built on SUNDIALS/CVODE. Time integration uses the variable-order BDF method, which suits the stiffness of coupled defect kinetics: the rates span many decades, and the physical times range from microseconds to \f$10^8\f$ s.

The Python layer precomputes all rate constants, writes them to a parameter file, starts the solver as a subprocess, and reads the solution back. The bridge is radcluster_code/py_utils/cpp_bridge.py.

\section Solver_intro_pages Pages

